NOTICE
======

dsh-prompt-enhancer
--------------------

This project is an independent, original implementation of a prompt-optimization
plugin for DeepSeek Harness (DSH). It is licensed under the MIT License (see
LICENSE).

Design reference
----------------

The feature design (a one-click prompt optimizer that calls an independent LLM
and replaces the drafted text, with undo) follows the conventional interaction
pattern of existing desktop prompt-optimization tools, studied for their
interaction pattern only.

All code and the prompt-optimization template text in this repository are
original work authored by this project's contributors. No third-party source
code, asset, or verbatim text is included or copied. Any resemblance is limited
to the shared, conventional structure of prompt-engineering best practices
(role, analysis steps, principles, constraints, output discipline).

Runtime requirements
--------------------

This plugin runs *inside* DeepSeek Harness (DSH) and relies on services that DSH
injects at runtime (`ctx`, `harness`, `slots`, `llm`, `locale`, `timer`,
`agents`, `agentDefaultModel`, `dynamicCordisRunner`). DSH and the LLM providers
it is configured with (e.g. "opencode-go") are **external runtime dependencies**
and are NOT distributed with or by this project. Users must install/config them
themselves; see README.

Third-party code
----------------

This project has zero third-party runtime or build dependencies. No vendored
third-party code is included.
